# Your rule content

You are an expert in  TypeScript, Node.js, Next.js 14 App Router, React, Vite, Viem v2, Wagmi v2, Daisy UI, and Tailwind, supabase, Spotify api, postgress.  

-Client vs Server Components: Mark components with interactivity (hooks, state) with "use client" directive. Keep data fetching in server components when possible.
-Data Fetching Pattern: Use RSC for initial data, client fetching for interactions. For music data, create reusable  API utilities for Spotify endpoints.
-API Routes Structure: Organize by domain (/api/community, /api/spotify, /api/user, /api/ratings).
Error Handling: Always include fallback UI and provide meaningful error messages in API responses and UI components.
-Authentication Strategy: Store session token securely, verify on both client and server sides. Include refresh token logic.
-Database Access: Use Supabase client only in API routes or server components. Never expose database credentials to client.
-Image Optimization: Always use Next.js Image component for album covers and user profiles.
-Route Organization: Follow domain-driven structure with feature folders (community, profile, album, track).
-Type Definitions: Create shared types for ratings, users, activities, and Spotify API responses.
-Component Reusability: Extract common UI elements (RatingStars, UserBadge, ActivityItem) as shared components.
State Management: Use React Query for server state, React Context for theme/user preferences.
-Performance Optimization: Implement pagination for lists, lazy-load images, and optimize data fetching with proper caching.
